    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "The crash-path removal is now installed.\n\nThe fatal `_SHOW_TOOLTIP` call and its `_CREATE_VAR_STRING` preparation are completely absent from the campsite code. I did not pad the structs, defer the call, or try the same undocumented ABI a third time. Holding F3 still performs the saved-row deletion, marker removal, exact physical `player_camp` cleanup request, and CSV persistence; the result is written to the unified log without any UI native.\n\nPlease test only this boundary: hold F3 at the campsite. It must not produce `ERROR:FFFFFFFF`, and the saved marker/row and physical camp must disappear. The cosmetic on-screen status notification is intentionally omitted in this build because both implementations of that notification caused the fatal call; I am not claiming that cosmetic requirement is solved.",
